---
/**
 * /provenance/: the event log, the ordered record a run carries across regimes,
 * physics domains and branches.
 *
 * Both excerpts are quoted verbatim from committed run output: the corridor's
 * blackout window (corridor/output.txt:56-63) and fourteen consecutive entries of
 * the retropropulsion descent (retropropulsion/output.txt:56-69). The leg table is read
 * off the corridor's per-leg summary lines.
 */
import PageShell from '../../components/nav/PageShell.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import { rustDark, rustLight } from '../../../shiki-rust-themes.mjs';
import { EXAMPLES_URL } from '../../consts';

const SHIKI = { light: rustLight, dark: rustDark };

const title = 'The event log | DeepCausality CFD';
const description =
  'One append-only event log continues across regime changes, across physics domains and across a fan-out of branches, so a question such as when the filter went blind reads off one sequence.';

/** corridor/output.txt:56-63, verbatim. The blackout window. */
const blackoutLog = `regime -> slip (GNSS-available), Kn=0.0771427732055074
nav: aided (position fix folded)
regime -> continuum (GNSS-available), Kn=0.009969942075728244
regime -> continuum (GNSS-denied), Kn=0.008711413345447542
nav: dead reckoning (no usable fix)
march paused at step 106
leg re-seeded from step 106 in world 'fine_bank_07': coupled field carried, marched fluid state re-seeded from the world seed
!!ContextAlternation!!: world 'nominal_descent' replaced with 'fine_bank_07'`;

/** retropropulsion/output.txt:56-69, verbatim. */
const retroLog = `regime -> continuum (GNSS-available), Kn=0.00015413843921263738, supersonic / thrust-unknown
nav: aided (position fix folded)
ignition corridor committed at step 2145: Mach 1.9987804348378688, q 2903.0349950149075 Pa, nav aided, sigma 0.3816520325841674 m
march paused at step 2146
leg re-seeded from step 2146 in world 'measured_day': coupled field carried, marched fluid state re-seeded from the world seed
regime -> continuum (GNSS-available), Kn=0.000014152129294753863, supersonic / burn
regime -> continuum (GNSS-available), Kn=0.000006464361502077825, transonic / burn
regime -> continuum (GNSS-available), Kn=0.0000032407604194220554, subsonic / burn
march paused at step 693
leg re-seeded from step 693 in world 'terminal_descent': coupled field carried, marched fluid state re-seeded from the world seed
carrier rebuilt at step 1: s_ref 1.4 -> 2.768213007453753 (rebuild 1)
SRP drag closure inert: no throttle commanded, no decrement applied
stopping burn started at step 2408: altitude 146.9058807976544 m, speed 48.65357396862805 m/s, thrust-to-weight 2.827727679713093
regime -> continuum (GNSS-available), Kn=0.00000018791887261341214, subsonic / burn, touchdown`;

/** Read straight off the corridor's per-leg summary lines. */
const legs = [
  { leg: 'Blackout starts, 76.8 km', link: 'GNSS denied', err: '0.3143 m', var: '2.739e-1 m²' },
  { leg: 'Peak passage, 61.0 km', link: 'GNSS denied', err: '3.0698 m', var: '2.778e2 m²' },
  { leg: 'Blackout ends, 45.7 km', link: 'GNSS available', err: '1.5585 m', var: '3.000e0 m²' },
  { leg: 'Reacquisition, 46.3 km', link: 'GNSS available', err: '0.2043 m', var: '3.226e-1 m²' },
];

const entries = [
  {
    name: 'regime',
    text: 'The flow classifier changed its verdict. The entry gives the Knudsen number (the ratio of the molecular mean free path to a length scale), the link state (GNSS, satellite navigation, available or denied) and, on the retropropulsion descent, the Mach band and the thrust state. The three burn-phase entries show the Mach band cascading from supersonic to transonic to subsonic.',
  },
  {
    name: 'nav',
    text: 'The navigation filter changed mode: aided when it folds in a position fix, dead reckoning when no usable fix exists.',
  },
  {
    name: 'march paused',
    text: 'A march stopped because its condition became true. The step number says when.',
  },
  {
    name: 'leg re-seeded',
    text: 'The run continued as a new leg, one stretch of the descent between pauses, in the named world. The coupled field carried over, bringing the navigation state and this log with it. The marched fluid state restarted from the world’s seed.',
  },
  {
    name: '!!ContextAlternation!!',
    text: 'The marker a branch stamps when its world replaces another. It names both worlds, so a what-if is auditable rather than implied.',
  },
  {
    name: 'ignition corridor committed',
    text: 'Guidance committed to ignition. The entry quotes the Mach number and dynamic pressure at the commit and the navigation filter’s own position uncertainty (sigma), so the decision carries its reason.',
  },
  {
    name: 'carrier rebuilt',
    text: 'The compressible solver rebuilt its carrier, the object that holds the marched layer, for a new reference wave speed s_ref. The entry gives the old and new values and counts the rebuilds.',
  },
  {
    name: 'SRP drag closure inert',
    text: 'The supersonic-retropropulsion (SRP) drag closure reports that it applied nothing: no throttle was commanded, so no decrement was applied. It logs its inertness rather than applying nothing silently.',
  },
  {
    name: 'stopping burn started',
    text: 'Terminal guidance started the landing burn. The entry gives altitude, speed and thrust-to-weight at that moment.',
  },
];
---
<PageShell title={title} description={description} path="/provenance/">
  <header class="doc-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Event log</p>
    <h1>The event log</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The link dropped: when did the filter go blind? The event log records every regime change,
      navigation mode change, pause and branch of a run in one ordered sequence, so you read the
      answer off it.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="doc-sec" id="ask">
    <h2>When did the filter go blind?</h2>
    <p>
      The corridor log answers in two adjacent entries. The flow classifier reports the link
      denied, and the next entry is the navigation filter falling back to dead reckoning. The
      march then pauses at step 106, at 76.8 km. Nothing scheduled that; the plasma chemistry
      located it.
    </p>

    <Code code={blackoutLog} lang="text" themes={SHIKI} />

    <p>
      The code calls this record the provenance log, or <code>EffectLog</code>. Every entry on this
      page is copied from a committed run.
    </p>
    <p>
      The last entry names both sides of an intervention: the world replaced,
      <code>nominal_descent</code>, and the world that replaced it, <code>fine_bank_07</code>. That
      world is the 11° bank angle the run committed. A what-if is therefore auditable, not
      implied.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-sec" id="entries">
    <h2>What does each entry mean?</h2>
    <p>
      Every stage that changes the story of a run appends one entry. These are fourteen consecutive
      entries from the committed retropropulsion descent, which carries twenty-two in total:
    </p>

    <Code code={retroLog} lang="text" themes={SHIKI} />

    <dl class="deflist">
      {entries.map((e) => (
        <div>
          <dt><code>{e.name}</code></dt>
          <dd>{e.text}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <p>
      Flow regime, navigation, guidance, solver and drag closure write into the same sequence. That
      is one chain to read, not several logs to correlate afterwards.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-sec" id="transition">
    <h2>Can you read one quantity on both sides of a transition?</h2>
    <p>
      Yes. The log spans the transition, so the same quantity reads on both sides of it. The
      corridor’s navigation error through the blackout, as committed:
    </p>

    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="table-stack">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Leg</th>
            <th scope="col">Link</th>
            <th scope="col">Error vs truth</th>
            <th scope="col">Position variance</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {legs.map((l) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{l.leg}</th>
              <td data-label="Link">{l.link}</td>
              <td class="num" data-label="Error vs truth">{l.err}</td>
              <td class="num" data-label="Position variance">{l.var}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p>
      Error vs truth is the filter’s position error against the simulated trajectory. Position
      variance is the filter’s own uncertainty. It grows by three orders of magnitude in the dark,
      then comes back once fixes resume.
    </p>
    <p>
      The retropropulsion descent supports the same reading across a Mach boundary. It logs
      supersonic, transonic and subsonic entries in one sequence with the thrust state on each
      line, so the flow parameters before and after the transition sit in the same record.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-sec" id="branches">
    <h2>Can you diff one branch against another?</h2>
    <p>
      Yes. Each branch of a fan-out carries its own event log, so a variant that failed can be
      diffed against one that passed instead of re-run under a debugger. The weather table gates on
      this: every dispersion world must carry the marker naming its baseline.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where a campaign uses the coupled <code>march_for</code> path, an optional
      <code>save_log(path)</code> flushes the log to disk: one file per branch, plus a
      <code>.main.log</code> naming every spawn and rejoin. The <code>fork</code> /
      <code>branch</code> / <code>continue_for</code> chain does not thread that sink and writes no
      files. Those branches carry their full event log in the returned report.
    </p>

    <ul class="nums">
      <li>Corridor descent: 16 entries covering four legs, two regime bands and one committed what-if.</li>
      <li>Retropropulsion descent: 22 entries covering blackout, ignition commit, a carrier rebuild, the stopping burn and touchdown.</li>
      <li>Weather table: 48 descents, each carrying its own log, gated on the <code>!!ContextAlternation!!</code> marker naming its baseline.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="next-links">
      <a href="/tutorial/stage-2-weather/">Walk 2: one baseline, six worlds</a>
      <a href="/blueprints/fork-a-running-simulation/">Blueprint: fork a running simulation</a>
      <a href={EXAMPLES_URL}>The committed run output <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </p>
  </section>
</PageShell>

<style>
  .doc-sec :global(pre.astro-code) { max-width: none; }

  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: var(--t-body-sm); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: var(--space-3); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-1); }
  thead th {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-eyebrow);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-eyebrow);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fg-2);
    font-weight: 400;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  tbody th { font-weight: 400; }
  tbody td { color: var(--fg-1); }
  tbody tr:last-child th, tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  tbody tr { transition: background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out); }
  tbody tr:hover { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 5%, transparent); }

  .nums { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); padding: 0; display: grid; gap: var(--space-2); }
  .doc-sec > ul.nums { padding-left: 0; }
  .nums li {
    color: var(--fg-1);
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: var(--space-3);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    font-size: var(--t-mono-sm);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
</style>
